 "intro": "The weather station on the summit has been automated for forty years. This morning its printer woke up and produced something that is definitely not a forecast. The forecasters, who still come up for the long nights out of habit, found the print-out lying under the teletype tray, where the morning's sheets always land, each slot in the rack fitted to receive just one width of paper. They stood around it a while, hands in pockets, not saying much — the kind of silence you get when something familiar has been arranged in a way nobody would call deliberate.",
 "echo": "The winds turn anticlockwise here, and clockwise on the other side of the world.",
